{% endblock %}
{% block budgets_guidance %}
{#
  BUDGETS. A summary a person approving the plan reads in a minute, often on a phone: what
  the plan is sized for, what breaks first at 10x, which budgets it adds, which it changes
  and from what, how much longer every change's checks take because of it, and which
  existing budgets already cover the work. Every detail of a budget — its workload,
  evidence, command and budgets file, and for a changed one its full before and after —
  lives in the `## Budgets` section of the task that owns it, which each row and line links
  to, and every plan-level answer in full lives in the plan's own description. So this
  section carries none of that detail. Each link is the budget's `link` answer as it
  stands: a standard `<path>#<slug>` link to the owning task's `### Budget <id>` heading,
  relative to this document's file when the task is a local file, never a
  `#user-content-` fragment and never anchor markup; a tracker's own form is the plan
  copy's to write. A budget answer saved before `link` existed is linked at its
  `location`, with `#` and its `anchor` when it carries one, so a document saved then
  still renders its own body.

  The answers `plan_budgets` and `budgets` are exactly the plan's records: the project's
  `orchestrator.plan-budgets` metadata and every task's `orchestrator.budgets`, each budget
  with its task and where the store reports it, a version-3 changed budget's `previous`
  inside it. Copy them, and invent none. A plan with no added or changed task budget (no
  `file_change` exactly `add` or `change`) renders no Budgets section, even when it has
  unchanged budgets, effects, omissions, spike findings or a migration reason. Otherwise
  the section shows, in order, each part only when it has entries: Sizing; At 10×; the
  added budgets; the changed budgets whose `name`, `unit`, `direction` or `threshold`
  differs from `previous`, plus every changed budget with no `previous`, each showing
  previous → new for a moved name or target and saying when its previous value is not
  recorded; one collapsed block counting the version-3 changed budgets that differ in
  another field, one line each naming, without values, which of measure, inner measure
  reason, workload, command and measurement source (`source`) differ, or check runtime
  when that is its only other difference; the total check runtime the budgets add,
  followed by `check_runtime_summary`; the relevant unchanged (`file_change: none`)
  budgets, collapsed as existing coverage of the work; then in-scope Not budgeted and
  Spike findings. Every table has two columns, budget and target. The total sums each
  added version-3 budget's `check_runtime_seconds` and each changed version-3 budget's
  `check_runtime_seconds` minus its `previous` one, adds nothing for an unchanged budget,
  names a displayed budget with no version-3 figure as not estimated (showing no figure
  when none has one), and shows a negative total as a saving. Repo-wide effects never appear here. Filtering is presentation only:
  copy all three answers in full, including unchanged budgets and effects.
#}
{% endblock %}
{% block budgets %}
{#- A budget's target as one cell, ≤ or ≥ before its threshold and unit. -#}
{% macro target(one) %}{% if one.direction == "min" %}≥{% else %}≤{% endif %}{{ one.threshold }} {{ cell(one.unit) }}{% endmacro %}
{#- Where a budget's name links: its owning task's budget heading. -#}
{% macro href(one) %}{% if one.link is defined %}{{ one.link }}{% else %}{{ one.location }}{% if one.anchor | default("") %}#{{ one.anchor }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{#- Seconds as a person reads them: whole when whole, else to one decimal place. -#}
{% macro seconds(value) %}{% if value == (value | int) %}{{ value | int }}{% else %}{{ value | round(1) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% set groups = namespace(added=[], rows=[], others=[], covering=[], unestimated=[], total=0, estimated=false) %}
{% for budget in budgets %}
{% set versioned = (budget.schema_version | default(0)) == 3 %}
{% if budget.file_change == "add" %}
{% set groups.added = groups.added + [budget] %}
{% if versioned %}
{% set groups.estimated = true %}
{% set groups.total = groups.total + budget.check_runtime_seconds %}
{% else %}
{% set groups.unestimated = groups.unestimated + [budget.name] %}
{% endif %}
{% elif budget.file_change == "change" %}
{% if versioned and budget.previous is defined %}
{% set was = budget.previous %}
{% set groups.estimated = true %}
{% set groups.total = groups.total + budget.check_runtime_seconds - was.check_runtime_seconds %}
{% if was.name != budget.name or was.unit != budget.unit or was.direction != budget.direction or was.threshold != budget.threshold %}
{% set groups.rows = groups.rows + [budget] %}
{% endif %}
{% set fields = namespace(names=[]) %}
{% for key, label in [["measure", "measure"], ["inner_measure_reason", "inner measure reason"], ["workload", "workload"], ["command", "command"], ["source", "measurement source"]] if was[key] != budget[key] %}
{% set fields.names = fields.names + [label] %}
{% endfor %}
{% if not fields.names and was.check_runtime_seconds != budget.check_runtime_seconds %}
{% set fields.names = ["check runtime"] %}
{% endif %}
{% if fields.names %}
{% set groups.others = groups.others + [{"budget": budget, "fields": fields.names}] %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% set groups.rows = groups.rows + [budget] %}
{% set groups.unestimated = groups.unestimated + [budget.name] %}
{% endif %}
{% elif budget.file_change == "none" %}
{% set groups.covering = groups.covering + [budget] %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set omissions = namespace(items=[]) %}
{% for entry in (plan_budgets.checklist | default([])) if entry.not_applicable and (entry.in_scope | default(false)) == true %}
{% set omissions.items = omissions.items + [entry] %}
{% endfor %}
{% if groups.added or (budgets | selectattr("file_change", "equalto", "change") | list) %}
## Budgets

**Sizing.** {{ plan_budgets.sizing }}

**At 10×.** {{ plan_budgets.ten_x_summary }}

{% if groups.added %}
**Added budgets:**

| Budget | Target |
| --- | --- |
{% for budget in groups.added %}
| [{{ cell(budget.name) }}][{{ loop.index }}] | {{ target(budget) }} |
{% endfor %}

{% for budget in groups.added %}
[{{ loop.index }}]: {{ href(budget) }}{{ "\n" -}}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if groups.rows %}
**Changed budgets:**

| Budget | Target |
| --- | --- |
{% for budget in groups.rows %}
{% set was = budget.previous if ((budget.schema_version | default(0)) == 3 and budget.previous is defined) else none %}
| [{% if was and was.name != budget.name %}{{ cell(was.name) }} → {% endif %}{{ cell(budget.name) }}][{{ groups.added | length + loop.index }}] | {% if not was %}{{ target(budget) }}, previous not recorded{% elif was.unit != budget.unit or was.direction != budget.direction or was.threshold != budget.threshold %}{{ target(was) }} → {{ target(budget) }}{% else %}{{ target(budget) }}{% endif %} |
{% endfor %}

{% for budget in groups.rows %}
[{{ groups.added | length + loop.index }}]: {{ href(budget) }}{{ "\n" -}}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if groups.others %}
<details>
<summary>{{ groups.others | length }} {% if groups.others | length == 1 %}budget{% else %}budgets{% endif %} changed for other reasons</summary>

{% for other in groups.others %}
- [{{ other.budget.name }}]({{ href(other.budget) }}): {{ other.fields | join(", ") }}
{% endfor %}

</details>

{% endif %}
**Check runtime added:** {% if not groups.estimated %}not estimated for {{ groups.unestimated | join("; ") }}{% else %}{% if groups.total < 0 %}saves ≈{{ seconds(0 - groups.total) }} s{% else %}≈{{ seconds(groups.total) }} s{% endif %}{% if groups.unestimated %}, not estimated for {{ groups.unestimated | join("; ") }}{% endif %}{% endif %}.{% if plan_budgets.check_runtime_summary | default("") %} {{ plan_budgets.check_runtime_summary }}{% endif %}


{% if groups.covering %}
<details>
<summary>{{ groups.covering | length }} existing {% if groups.covering | length == 1 %}budget already covers{% else %}budgets already cover{% endif %} this work</summary>

| Budget | Target |
| --- | --- |
{% for budget in groups.covering %}
| [{{ cell(budget.name) }}]({{ href(budget) }}) | {{ target(budget) }} |
{% endfor %}

</details>

{% endif %}
{% if omissions.items %}
**Not budgeted:**

{% for entry in omissions.items %}
- {{ entry.concern }}: {{ entry.summary }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% for entry in (plan_budgets.spike_findings | default([])) %}
{% if loop.first %}
**Spike findings:**

{% endif %}
- {{ entry.summary }}
{% if loop.last %}

